==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*5 [[Haniwanwan]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 86.67~90 seconds<sup>2,600f~2,700f</sup>.
*10 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
*5 [[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gories]] spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 50~53.33 seconds<sup>1,500f~1,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Casaurian Darkjo]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Infernal Pegasus Deonil]] spawns as the boss after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Red EnerG]] spawns after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 300 seconds<sup>9,000f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
As with many other [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] stages, [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] is going to work wonders, killing the Ragin' Gories, while being able to get in an occasional hit on Deonil, and doing loads of damage to Red EnerG. [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] is also great here, with their high range and [[Multi-Hit]] doing high chip damage to Deonil and Darkjo as well as the peons. You could use Darkjo and other peons as a stepping stone for Naala, keeping them safe from Deonil.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N206 (Special Cat)|Clam Cat]] - Clam Cat resists Red and Dark enemies, has Behemoth Slayer, and Knockback Immunity, giving them great matchups against the main threats in this level. Additionally, if they're boosted with both [[Catseye]]s and +levels, they can survive an [[Iguanidae Ibilujon|Iguanidae]] attack at Lv.50+4, an [[H. Nah]] attack at Lv.50+5 and a 200% Wild Doge attack at Lv.50+9, which makes them much more useful for Yellow Crystal Volcano.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - Given his [[Massive Damage]] against Red enemies, as well as Behemoth Slayer, Courier Cat is well-suited to deal with every enemy in this stage. However, boosting him is recommended: the lower his level, the fewer the hits he can take before getting knocked back and eventually succumbing to Deonil's Mini-Waves and Red EnerG's Surge Attacks. He can also serve as somewhat decent source of chip damage for enemies in the subsequent Continuation Stage.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]] - Lunacia is Strong against Red EnerG, Deonil and Haniwanwan, and can block the [[Wave Attack#Mini-Wave|Mini-Waves]] of the latter two as well. She also has a guaranteed Freeze against her traits, making it much easier for Courier to attack Deonil. She is vulnerable to Red EnerG's Surges and Darkjo's Toxic, so use her wisely.
*[[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Dawnbringer Izanagi]]: If you stall the frontliners you can use them as a stepping stone for Izanagi to hit the Deonil and can eliminate him before the Red EnerG spawns.

==Trivia==
*The names of this stage, and its prequel stage, [[Yellow Stone Volcano III]], are potentially a reference to [[wikipedia:Yellowstone Caldera|Yellowstone Caldera]]: otherwise known as the Yellowstone Supervolcano. Situated beneath Yellowstone National Park in Wyoming, it is best known for its current status of dormancy despite its overwhelmingly destructive potential if it were to erupt today.

